# chmod — change file permissions

## Symbolic mode

```sh
# Add execute for all
chmod a+x myscript.sh

# User read/write/execute, group/global read only
chmod u=rwx,go=r myscript.sh

# Remove write from everyone
chmod a-w myscript.sh

# Strip all permissions
chmod = myscript.sh
```

## Octal notation

```sh
chmod 644 notes.txt       # user rw, group/global r
chmod 755 myscript.sh     # user rwx, group/global rx
chmod 666 shared.txt      # everyone rw
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/config   # user rw only
```

## Directories

```sh
chmod 755 /opt/myapp

# Recursive
chmod -R 755 /opt/myapp
```

## Real-world: fix a fresh SSH setup

```sh
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ~/.ssh/config
chmod 644 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

## Real-world: make Plex media readable, scripts runnable

```sh
find ~/Media -type d -exec chmod 755 {} +
find ~/Media -type f -exec chmod 644 {} +
chmod +x ~/scripts/*.py
```

## Roles

| Letter | Who                                         |
| ------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| u      | user (owner of the file)                    |
| g      | group (members of file's group)             |
| o      | global (everyone else)                      |
| a      | all three roles above                       |

## Numeric values

| Value | Permissions              |
| ----- | ------------------------ |
| 7     | full (rwx)               |
| 6     | read and write (rw-)     |
| 5     | read and execute (r-x)   |
| 4     | read only (r--)          |
| 3     | write and execute (-wx)  |
| 2     | write only (-w-)         |
| 1     | execute only (--x)       |
| 0     | none (---)               |
